Your app allows you to record and listen to your voice because **audio recording (`MediaRecorder`) and audio playback (`MediaPlayer`) operate locally on your phone's storage**. 

However, **Speech-to-Text conversion (`SpeechRecognizer`) and Pronunciation Scoring fail** because your app attempts to start both `MediaRecorder` and Android's `SpeechRecognizer` at the exact same time. On physical Android phones, **the microphone cannot be captured simultaneously by two different components**, causing `SpeechRecognizer` to receive no audio input and return empty text.

